<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>More Related Works</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we discuss more related works to supplement the main text.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning</span>. Large language models (LLMs) are often post-trained using reinforcement learning (RL), both for preference alignment <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022</a>]</cite> and to improve reasoning capabilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>]</cite>. Inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al. [2024]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu [2025]</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Swamy et al. [2025]</a></cite>, this work reformulates methods like SFT, RFT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Trung et al., 2024</a>]</cite>, DPO, PPO, and GRPO as maximum likelihood estimation governed by a <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gradient Coefficient</span>. This coefficient fundamentally operates by amplifying gradients for favored responses and suppressing others, with its magnitude modulating the preference intensity. Thus, the core challenge in policy gradient methods reduces to the accurate estimation of this <span id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gradient Coefficient</span> (i.e., the advantage and importance ratio). For instance, AAPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2025a</a>]</cite> redefines advantage estimation by incorporating advantage momentum. GAPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>]</cite>, GVPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>]</cite> and <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math> Normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025b</a>]</cite> employ gradient normalization to adaptively rescale each objective’s gradients, thereby finding a low-variance estimator. Meanwhile, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. [2025b]</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qian et al. [2025]</a></cite> utilize a model’s own internal confidence measure (or entropy)—termed self-certainty to improve reasoning skills. Additionally, hybrid approaches that integrate RL with SFT on external demonstration data have been actively explored <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2025</a>]</cite>. Despite these empirical advances, the fundamental question of whether RLVR expands <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wen et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yuan et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2025</a>]</cite> or shrinks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yue et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dang et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025a</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shah et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandhi et al., 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dang et al., 2025b</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">O’Mahony et al., 2024</a>]</cite> the reasoning capacities of LLMs remains an open and actively debated issue. <span id="A1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This is precisely what we aim to uncover</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Learning Dynamics</span>. Deep neural networks learn by adjusting their parameters through gradient descent. This process, known as learning dynamics, connects how model predictions change to the gradients from individual training examples. <span id="A1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Learning dynamics prioritizes the analysis of a model’s relative training behavior over its convergence, providing a means to assess the quality of individual training samples</span>. To name a few, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pruthi et al. [2020]</a></cite> introduce “TracIn", a metric that measures how much a training example affects a model’s predictions, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al. [2024]</a></cite> later use it to identify the most influential examples during instruction fine-tuning of LLMs. In a similar vein, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. [2024]</a></cite> propose a method based on the neural tangent kernel (NTK) regime to estimate the relative difficulty among different training samples. Furthermore, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren and Sutherland [2025]</a></cite> highlight a unique “squeezing effect” to explain a previously observed phenomenon in off-policy direct preference optimization (DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024</a>]</cite>), where running DPO for too long makes even the desired outputs less likely. Since RLVR methods—exemplified by PPO and GRPO—are on-policy and dynamically evolving, we argue that analyzing learning dynamics can naturally offer a novel perspective for understanding the hot debate (capability boundary shrinkage or expansion) in RLVR.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Analysis in Preference Optimization</span>. DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024</a>]</cite> has proven highly effective, as it relies solely on an offline dataset of paired preference data. However, this reliance on paired data restricts its applicability in settings where only unpaired feedback (e.g., solely positive or negative responses) is available. In response, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abdolmaleki et al. [2025]</a></cite> introduce a decoupled approach that independently controls the influence of positive and negative signals, enabling learning even when only a single feedback type is available. Regarding online update methods, RAFT++ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2023</a>, <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2025b</a>]</cite>—a simple rejection sampling approach utilizing only positively rewarded data—has been shown to deliver performance competitive with GRPO. Conversely, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. [2025b]</a></cite> report the surprising effectiveness of training exclusively on negatively rewarded samples using REINFORCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams, 1992</a>]</cite>, without reinforcing correct responses. <span id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As we demonstrate in the main text, the set of samples considered “negative" is not static but evolves dynamically throughout optimization</span>. It imperative to analyze the underlying learning dynamics. In addition, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. [2025a]</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. [2025a]</a></cite> find that negative responses hold learning value (e.g., self-reflection). However, existing methods overlook this by either discarding them (RFT) or applying uniform penalties (RL), failing to leverage these nuanced signals. There are also some token-level gradient analyses: <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. [2025b]</a></cite> identify that RL training is skewed by low-probability tokens’ excessive gradient magnitudes, impeding the learning from essential high-probability tokens; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. [2025]</a></cite> empirically observe that GRPO can suffer from what we call Lazy Likelihood Displacement: a failure to sufficiently increase, or even a decrease in, the likelihood of correct answers during training. <span id="A1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above motivates us to analyze the expected update in RLVR, once again emphasizing the essential role of fine-grained probability mass allocation</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">LLM Usage</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Regarding the use of LLMs, they were employed solely for language polishing purposes and played no role in research ideation, literature retrieval, or any other academically substantive activities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Omitted Proofs and Additional Results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Equation 2</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by reviewing the objective function of GRPO below.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\left\{\min\left(w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t},\text{clip}\big(w_{i,t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\big)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right)\right\}-\beta\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>clip</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\left\{\min\left(w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t},\text{clip}\big(w_{i,t}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon\big)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right)\right\}-\beta\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i,t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})},\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})=\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}-\log\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})},\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})=\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}-\log\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the coefficient.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To better understand the model’s learning dynamics under this binary outcome reward setting, we
omit the regularization components (e.g., KL term &amp; clipping operation):</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}\hat{A}_{i,t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}\hat{A}_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})}\hat{A}_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\underbrace{w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}}_{\text{coefficient }}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>coefficient </mtext></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\ \{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\underbrace{w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}}_{\text{coefficient }}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We complete the proof of Equation <a href="#A2.Ex10" title="Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Equation 2 ‣ Appendix B Omitted Proofs and Additional Results ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. Notice that <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> does not affect the sign of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Besides, one can also consider the gradient of the KL term (denote <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\beta\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\beta\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\theta}\mid\mid\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\nabla_{\theta}\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}-\beta\nabla_{\theta}\log\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\nabla_{\theta}\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}-\beta\nabla_{\theta}\log\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\beta\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi^{2}_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})+\beta\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\beta\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi^{2}_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})+\beta\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\left[\beta\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}-\beta\right]\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\left[\beta\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t})}-\beta\right]\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Lemma 1</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Re-stating the Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the output of a model is the logits <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=[z_{1},...,z_{V}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=[z_{1},...,z_{V}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to a finite (size <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>) vocabulary set <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},...,v_{V}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},...,v_{V}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The policy probability of the corresponding action (token) is calculated by: <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(v)=\text{Softmax}(\mathbf{z})_{v}=\exp{(z_{v})}/\sum^{V}_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}\exp{(z_{v^{{}^{\prime}}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Softmax</mtext><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(v)=\text{Softmax}(\mathbf{z})_{v}=\exp{(z_{v})}/\sum^{V}_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}\exp{(z_{v^{{}^{\prime}}})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">That is, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\pi(v)=\log(\exp(z_{v}))-\log(\sum_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}^{V}\exp(z_{v}^{{}^{\prime}}))=z_{v}-\log(\sum_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}^{V}\exp(z_{v}^{{}^{\prime}}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi(v)=\log(\exp(z_{v}))-\log(\sum_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}^{V}\exp(z_{v}^{{}^{\prime}}))=z_{v}-\log(\sum_{v^{{}^{\prime}}}^{V}\exp(z_{v}^{{}^{\prime}})).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for the currently sampled token <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> be its corresponding logit, we will have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\log\pi(v)}{\partial z_{v}}=1-\pi(v)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\log\pi(v)}{\partial z_{v}}=1-\pi(v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">for other unsampled tokens <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\neq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\neq v</annotation></semantics></math> (with its logit <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\log\pi(v)}{\partial z_{u}}=-\pi(u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\log\pi(v)}{\partial z_{u}}=-\pi(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Apply those to the gradient <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\hat{A}(v)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\hat{A}(v)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, we complete the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proposition 1 and Proof</h3>

<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the conditions specified in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> hold, and denote <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}(\mathbf{x})=[\Delta z_{1},...,\Delta z_{V}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}(\mathbf{x})=[\Delta z_{1},...,\Delta z_{V}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th step probability mass dynamics decompose as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\left[I-\mathbf{e}(\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x})+\mathcal{O}(\eta^{2}\left\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\left[I-\mathbf{e}(\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x})+\mathcal{O}(\eta^{2}\left\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity matrix and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}=[1,1,...,1]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}=[1,1,...,1]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical neural tangent kernel, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}(\mathbf{x})=\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}(\mathbf{x})=\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which mainly determines the <span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">direction and magnitude</span> of the policy update.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the log probabilities change in Eq. (4):</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\log\pi_{\theta^{l+1}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi_{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}):=\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\log\pi_{\theta^{l+1}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi_{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}):=\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">and we follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren and Sutherland [2025]</a></cite> using Taylor expansion to approximate <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})+\langle\nabla\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}),\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\rangle+\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi^{l+1}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})+\langle\nabla\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}),\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\rangle+\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, supposing the parameters’ are updated by policy gradient, we will have (the model parameters <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l})+\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l})+\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we use the definition of gradient and the chain rule:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]\left[\eta\nabla_{\theta^{l}}\mathcal{J}\right]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]\left[\eta\nabla_{\theta^{l}}\mathcal{J}\right]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]\left[\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J}(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]\left[\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J}(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))\right]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right](\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\log\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right](\eta\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[I-\mathbf{e}(\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[I-\mathbf{e}(\pi^{l}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">For the higher-order term:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}=\eta\nabla_{\theta^{l}}\mathcal{J}=\eta(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}=\eta\nabla_{\theta^{l}}\mathcal{J}=\eta(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">and from the practical application and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the term <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}}\mathcal{J}</annotation></semantics></math> is usually bounded, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2})=\mathcal{O}(\eta^{2}\left\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{O}(\left\|\theta^{l+1}-\theta^{l}\right\|^{2})=\mathcal{O}(\eta^{2}\left\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">We complete the proof. <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))(\nabla_{\theta}\mathbf{z}^{\theta^{l}}(\mathbf{x}))^{T}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the empirical neural tangent kernel (NTK), which remains nearly constant throughout the training process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren and Sutherland, 2025</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2019</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jacot et al., 2018</a>]</cite>. As a result, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}^{l}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> primarily governs both the direction and magnitude of the policy update.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.</span> Under the conditions stated in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we assume that <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is i.i.d., the expected group relative policy gradient <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\hat{A}(u_{i})\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u_{i})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\hat{A}(u_{i})\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u_{i})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the expected logits update is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(\Delta z_{v}^{l})=\eta\cdot\mathbb{E}_{u\sim\pi^{l}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{z_{v}^{l}}\log\pi^{l}(u)\right]=\eta\cdot\pi^{l}(v)\left[(1-\pi^{l}(v))\hat{A}(v)-\sum_{u\neq v}\pi^{l}(u)\hat{A}(u)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></msub><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(\Delta z_{v}^{l})=\eta\cdot\mathbb{E}_{u\sim\pi^{l}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{z_{v}^{l}}\log\pi^{l}(u)\right]=\eta\cdot\pi^{l}(v)\left[(1-\pi^{l}(v))\hat{A}(v)-\sum_{u\neq v}\pi^{l}(u)\hat{A}(u)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the policy gradient of sampling a token (action) <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> once from the policy <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{l}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{l}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the expected group relative policy gradient is the following:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\hat{A}(u_{i})\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u_{i})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D},\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\hat{A}(u_{i})\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u_{i})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is i.i.d. and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> are randomly sampled from <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive an unbiased estimator:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbb{E}_{u\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)\right]=\sum_{u}\pi(u)\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\mathcal{J}=\mathbb{E}_{u\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)\right]=\sum_{u}\pi(u)\hat{A}(u)\nabla_{\mathbf{z}}\log\pi(u)\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times 1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Apply those to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization). ‣ 3.1 A Two-Stage Dynamic: Exploitation and Exploration ‣ 3 Probability Mass Dynamics ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Details of Relative Negative Gradients</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Referring back to Eq.(<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Preliminaries and Background ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#A2.Ex10" title="Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Equation 2 ‣ Appendix B Omitted Proofs and Additional Results ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), taking GRPO as an example, we obtain the gradient of the objective function in the following form.</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)\ =\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\underbrace{w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}}_{\text{coefficient }}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>coefficient </mtext></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)\ =\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\underbrace{w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}}_{\text{coefficient }}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the advantage <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated from the currently sampled group <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\cdots,G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\cdots,G</annotation></semantics></math> each time, we refer to it as the relative advantage, and correspondingly, this gradient is termed the relative policy gradient. Consequently, for the relative negative gradients, we exclusively utilize gradient information where <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> during the gradient update:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO-N}}(\theta)\ =\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\mathbb{I}(\hat{A}_{i,t})\cdot w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO-N</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO-N}}(\theta)\ =\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\{\mathbf{y}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x})}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|\mathbf{y}_{i}|}\mathbb{I}(\hat{A}_{i,t})\cdot w_{i,t}(\theta)\hat{A}_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{i,&lt;t})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(\hat{A}_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(\hat{A}_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator variable that equals 1 if <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and 0 otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Extension to Experiments</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reproducibility statement</span>. We employed open-source algorithms and data to validate our theoretical analysis, and have reported all hyperparameter settings to facilitate reproducibility.
<br class="ltx_break">(1) open-source code: <a href="https://github.com/volcengine/verl" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/volcengine/verl</a>.
<br class="ltx_break">(2) all datasets can be found in: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets</a>.
<br class="ltx_break">(3) toy example details are provided in: Algorithm <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Algorithm for Logits Update ‣ Appendix C Extension to Experiments ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Algorithm for Logits Update</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Logits Update for Softmax Parameterization: A Toy Example</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require:</span> learning rate <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, number of samples per update <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, true rewards <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            Initialize policy parameters (logits) <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Compute current policy <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\leftarrow\text{Softmax}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\leftarrow\text{Softmax}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> actions from policy <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{1},a_{2},...,a_{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{1},a_{2},...,a_{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Estimate advantage <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}[a_{i}]=r[a_{i}]-\text{mean}(\{r[a_{j}]\}_{j=1}^{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}[a_{i}]=r[a_{i}]-\text{mean}(\{r[a_{j}]\}_{j=1}^{G})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Initialize relative policy gradient <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}\leftarrow\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sampled action <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}[a_{i}]\leftarrow\mathbf{g}[a_{i}]+(1-\pi[a_{i}])\cdot\hat{A}[a_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}[a_{i}]\leftarrow\mathbf{g}[a_{i}]+(1-\pi[a_{i}])\cdot\hat{A}[a_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each other action <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}\neq a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}\neq a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}[a_{j}]\leftarrow\mathbf{g}[a_{j}]-\pi[a_{j}]\cdot\hat{A}[a_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}[a_{j}]\leftarrow\mathbf{g}[a_{j}]-\pi[a_{j}]\cdot\hat{A}[a_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Apply Adam update: <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}+\eta\cdot\mathbf{g}/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}+\eta\cdot\mathbf{g}/G</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> Optimized policy parameters <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Hyperparameter Settings</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our experimental configuration follows that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. [2025b]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training setup</span>.
The prompt batch size is set to 1,024, with 8 rollouts generated per prompt. During training, the sampling temperature is set to 1.0. The maximum context length is configured as 4,096 tokens for both <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen2.5-Math-7B</span> and <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct</span>. Model updates are performed with a mini-batch size of 256 and a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all algorithms, a KL penalty term is incorporated into the final loss function, using a coefficient of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>. The clip ratio is set to 0.2. Additionally, an entropy bonus is applied to all objectives with a coefficient of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. All experiments are conducted on a single node with 4 NVIDIA A100 GPUs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation setup</span>. During evaluation, we sample 256 responses per prompt for both <span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen2.5-Math-7B</span> and <span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct</span> using a temperature of 0.6 and a top<span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span><math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> value of 0.95. Since the test sets of ARC-c (1,170) and MMLU-Pro (12,000) are relatively large, and sampling 256 times requires substantial computation time, we randomly selected 128 questions and repeated the test three times to obtain the average.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt template</span>. Our primary objective is to validate theoretical findings; therefore, a uniform prompt <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng et al., 2025</a>]</cite> was sampled for all models:</p>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,PHxpbV9zdGFydHw+c3lzdGVtCllvdSBhcmUgYSBoZWxwZnVsIGFzc2lzdGFudC48fGltX2VuZHw+Cjx8aW1fc3RhcnR8PnVzZXIKe2lucHV0fQpQbGVhc2UgcmVhc29uIHN0ZXAgYnkgc3RlcCwgYW5kIHB1dCB5b3VyIGZpbmFsIGFuc3dlciB3aXRoaW4gXGJveGVke30uCjx8aW1fZW5kfD4KPHxpbV9zdGFydHw+YXNzaXN0YW50" download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">im_start</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">|&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">system</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">You</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">are</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">a</span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">helpful</span><span id="lstnumberx2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">assistant</span><span id="lstnumberx2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.&lt;|</span><span id="lstnumberx2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">im_end</span><span id="lstnumberx2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">|&gt;</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">im_start</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">|&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">user</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{</span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_lst_keywords2 ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">input</span><span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">}</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Please</span><span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">reason</span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">step</span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">by</span><span id="lstnumberx5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">step</span><span id="lstnumberx5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx5.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">and</span><span id="lstnumberx5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">put</span><span id="lstnumberx5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">your</span><span id="lstnumberx5.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">final</span><span id="lstnumberx5.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">answer</span><span id="lstnumberx5.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">within</span><span id="lstnumberx5.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\</span><span id="lstnumberx5.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">boxed</span><span id="lstnumberx5.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{}.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|</span><span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">im_end</span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">|&gt;</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|</span><span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">im_start</span><span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">|&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">assistant</span>
</div>
