</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Entropy Behavior Analysis from Different Levels</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set up.</span> To investigate how different algorithms reshapes the sampling distribution, we compare the base model with the RLVR trained model (using the experimental setup detailed in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 How to Prolong Training: Revisiting the Role of Relative Negative Gradients ‣ The Debate on RLVR Reasoning Capability Boundary: Shrinkage, Expansion, or Both? A Two-Stage Dynamic View" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. [2025a]</a></cite>, we quantify changes in the output distribution using two entropy metrics:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> Answer-Level Entropy: Let <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o^{(1)},\ldots,o^{(G)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o^{(1)},\ldots,o^{(G)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the answers extracted from each generated sequence <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (with NA denoting incomplete or invalid outputs), and let <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o_{1}^{*},\ldots,o_{M}^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o_{1}^{*},\ldots,o_{M}^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> distinct answers. Denote by <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> the frequency of answer <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{j}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{j}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the empirical probability as <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}=\frac{f_{j}}{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}=\frac{f_{j}}{G}</annotation></semantics></math>. The answer-level entropy is then defined as: <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{AnswerEntropy}=-\sum_{j=1}^{M}p_{j}\log p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>AnswerEntropy</mtext><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AnswerEntropy}=-\sum_{j=1}^{M}p_{j}\log p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. This metric quantifies the global diversity across output completions, where lower entropy values indicate a greater degree of answer-level certainty.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> Token-Level Entropy: Let <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the vocabulary and <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{i}=(y_{i,1},y_{i,2},\ldots,y_{i,T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{i}=(y_{i,1},y_{i,2},\ldots,y_{i,T})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th generated sequence of length <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>. At each timestep <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the model outputs a probability distribution <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(i)}_{t}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(i)}_{t}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> over vocabulary tokens <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. The entropy of this distribution is given by: <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(p^{(i)}_{t})=-\sum_{v\in\mathcal{V}}p^{(i)}_{t}(v)\log p^{(i)}_{t}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p^{(i)}_{t})=-\sum_{v\in\mathcal{V}}p^{(i)}_{t}(v)\log p^{(i)}_{t}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. The average token-level entropy over all <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> sequences and all timesteps is then computed as: <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TokenEntropy}=\frac{1}{G}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{T}H(p^{(i)}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>TokenEntropy</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TokenEntropy}=\frac{1}{G}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{T}H(p^{(i)}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
